# In July 2026, the Orchestre national d'Île-de-France goes to Japan on an exceptional tour

From 1 to 18 July 2026, the Orchestre national d'Île-de-France will travel for its first tour in Japan:

- 10 concerts in some of the country’s most prestigious venues, and 2 return concerts in Paris (Philharmonie de Paris and La Seine Musicale);

- 8 cities visited: Osaka, Takamatsu, Fukuoka, Tokyo, Sapporo, Nagoya, Hamamatsu, Musashino;

- More than 20,000 spectators expected.

This international tour, dedicated to artistic dialogue between France and Japan, will celebrate friendship and cultural exchange between the two countries.

The Orchestra is seeking partners to support this Japanese adventure.

Supporting this exceptional project offers companies the opportunity to associate their image with an artistic journey combining visibility, commitment and influence:

- A strong lever for image, influence and business opportunities;

- A prestigious partnership with an orchestra of excellence;

- A meaningful commitment in support of artistic creation and cultural cooperation;

- Enhanced visibility to develop business relationships;

- Attractive tax benefits and exclusive partner privileges.

Join the adventure and become a partner of the Orchestre national d'Île-de-France tour in Japan.

Information and contact: audrey.chauvelot(@)orchestre-ile.com

